WEBVTT

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:05.500
Everyone, when you're watching Deltora Quest,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.300
make sure you're in a well-lit
room and sit far away from the TV!

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:24.060
If I open this door, I'll find a new world

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:28.480
A world only just beginning

00:00:29.850 --> 00:00:34.730
Even if there are tough times ahead

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.120
I'm sure I'll make it through

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:48.540
Now I'm making my way through this new world

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:54.860
And I've got hopes and dreams

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.700
I'm excited, I'm restless

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.220
Nobody can stop me

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:01.260
My heart is all fired up
Nobody can stop me

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.390
My heart is all fired up

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.420
From here I'll leap into the world

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:10.480
Taking to the sky
From here I'll leap into the world

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:13.610
Taking to the sky

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:19.680
Aiming for tomorrow and beyond

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:26.060
I believe that someday I'll grow up

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:31.080
That's why I'll spread my wings wide

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:54.750
The Japanese Deltora Quest is brought to you in English by ToranSubs

00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.910
<i>My name is Lief.</i>

00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.210
<i>And I'm Jasmine.</i>

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:03.380
<i>We're currently travelling to seven perilous places in order to recover the seven stolen gems!</i>

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:07.390
<i>We've already acquired the topaz,
ruby, opal, and the lapis lazuli!</i>

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.900
<i>We had to face some monsters, but they weren't anything we couldn't handle!</i>

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.900
<i>Hey now, we don't know what kinds of enemies we'll have to face in the future. You both need to be careful.</i>

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.500
<i>Geez, you worry too much, Barda!</i>

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:24.210
<i>And right now, we're headed to
Dread Mountain where the fifth gem is located!</i>

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.900
<i>Fallow... Fallow..!</i>

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.390
Four of the seven gems have been stolen.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:41.200
Just what have you been
doing to put a stop to this?!

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.500
M-My sincerest apologies...!

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.260
A-Although, we do already
know the culprits' identities.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:54.200
It is a group of three; a brawny man,
a boy, and a girl with a black bird!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:57.600
Then why have you not moved to apprehend them?!

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.700
Fear not, my lord. I have already ordered the Grey Guards to scour the land far and wide.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:06.120
It is only a matter of time until they are caught.

00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:09.520
Naïve! You will dispatch the Carn Unit.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:12.380
The Carn Unit, my lord?

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.240
Dispatch them with haste!

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.000
Yes, my lord...

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.700
We're heading off.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.000
Let's rest for a moment.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.280
I'm exhausted...

00:03:56.710 --> 00:03:59.100
Do you still have water left, Jasmine?

00:04:00.630 --> 00:04:02.500
My flask is completely dry.

00:04:03.270 --> 00:04:04.330
As is mine.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:05.620
Mine too...

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:16.900
What's the matter, Lief?

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.220
Kree sure flew by quickly just then, didn't he?

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:22.000
What are you talking about?

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:25.350
Huh?

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.200
Is that true, Kree?!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:33.900
Good news, guys! Kree says that
there's a water source up ahead!

00:04:34.070 --> 00:04:35.240
That's great!

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.080
I can see it!

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:50.580
Thank goodness!

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:51.080
Yeah!

00:04:58.820 --> 00:04:59.920
We're almost there!

00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:03.420
It's a spring!

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.800
I don't recall tasting water this delicious before.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.050
It's cold and really sweet!

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:17.850
It is.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.600
Right then, let's rest here for the night.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:22.500
Yeah.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:24.950
Is something wrong, Jasmine?

00:05:26.270 --> 00:05:31.000
I'm not too sure, but it feels as
if the trees here are all dead...

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:32.400
Dead?

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:37.130
Even though they're all covered in healthy leaves?

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:42.100
I don't see anything unusual about them either.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.400
But... I'm getting a strange feeling here.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.200
A strange feeling?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.130
What's that?

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.900
"Dreaming Spring".

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:03.990
"Drink, gentle stranger, and welcome. All of evil will beware."

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:05.840
What does it mean?

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.200
Maybe it's some kind of message.

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:14.400
So in other words, evildoers will meet a bad end if they dare to drink the water from this spring?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.550
I wonder if it has poison in it or something...

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.050
P-Poison?!

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:25.810
Either way, panicking now won't do us any good. We've already drunk from this spring, after all.

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:29.700
Or do you actually think of
yourself as an 'evildoer', Lief?

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:31.500
Of course not!

00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:34.100
Then there's nothing to worry about, right?

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:34.850
Huh?

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:38.340
I'm saying that we'll be fine, since we're not bad guys.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:40.600
I guess you're right...

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:51.000
This is a good spot. We'll be more easily spotted by Grey Guards if we camp near the spring, after all.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:54.470
It is a little unfortunate that
we can't light a fire, though.

00:06:55.120 --> 00:07:01.920
I guess we've become more wary of our surroundings now, even though we used to be pretty carefree before...

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:07.140
Well, we can't afford to get caught before we gather the seven gems, after all.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.100
Exactly.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:10.820
Yeah, I know...

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:15.590
Alright, let's take turns keeping watch. I'll go first.

00:07:15.860 --> 00:07:18.600
Right. I can go next, then.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:20.050
As for Jasmine...

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:24.000
She's already sleeping...

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.200
You can't blame her.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.700
Just let her sleep for now.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.500
Yeah.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:37.720
Come to think of it, Jasmine did say that the trees here are dead, didn't she...?

00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:39.800
Don't let it worry you.

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:41.970
Look at Kree and Filli.

00:07:42.580 --> 00:07:48.220
They are sleeping soundly, aren't they? So, I'd say this place should be relatively safe.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:50.600
I see...

00:07:51.600 --> 00:07:52.540
I guess you're right.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:55.030
Now, get some sleep while you can.

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:56.310
Right. Good night.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:57.900
Good night.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.650
<i>I hope we can gather all of the
gems and return to Del soon...</i>

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:20.000
Isn't this... my house...?

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.200
A Kin doll...

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:38.200
Why is the toy that I had as a child here...?

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:46.200
T-This is...!

00:08:50.490 --> 00:08:53.100
Why is everything in this state?!

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:02.910
Father... Mother... Where are they?!

00:09:26.180 --> 00:09:31.200
A dream...? I would have preferred to
have had a more pleasant one, though...

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.290
Barda?

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:38.410
Barda? Barda?

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:41.900
We all were pretty exhausted.

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:57.200
A Kin?!

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.050
It couldn't be... A real Kin?!

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.910
So they <i>do</i> still exist...!

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.330
What do you mean by that?

00:10:18.460 --> 00:10:20.410
D-Did you just talk?!

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:23.400
That's right, I'm talking to you.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:25.350
Is something wrong?

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.900
N-Not really...

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:31.120
What's your name, Mister?

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:33.600
I'm Lief.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:36.310
My name is Prin!

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:38.520
That's a cute name.

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.400
Thanks!

00:10:40.400 --> 00:10:43.600
By the way, what did you
mean by 'they still exist'?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.500
Eh? Ah, it's just...

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.390
I had heard that the Kin had
died out long ago, you see.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:57.300
Died out? Then what do you think I am? There's no denying that I'm a Kin, you know?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.370
What do you say to that?

00:10:59.370 --> 00:11:05.030
O-Oh, no, I do believe that you're a real Kin, but it just feels like I'm still dreaming.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:09.800
Ouch! Ow ow ow ow ow! That hurts...

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.400
Guess I'm not dreaming...

00:11:14.270 --> 00:11:18.900
Dreaming? The only ones still
dreaming here are the adults. Look!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:23.700
Since when have they been there...

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:29.600
They usually won't wake up
until the sun is really high.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:37.130
Mum told me to stay put until everyone wakes up, but... that's just so boring...

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:42.590
Hey, Lief!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.500
Let's play together!

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:47.340
Sure!

00:11:47.490 --> 00:11:51.760
Yay! Then let's play hide-and-seek! You can hide first!

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:52.700
Okay!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.900
Then, let's start!

00:11:56.450 --> 00:12:03.650
Hide and seek! Hide and seek! I'll be the one to seek and will find wherever you hide!

00:12:03.650 --> 00:12:13.820
My sharp eyes are looking for you! No matter how well you're hidden, I will find you in the blink of an eye!

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.840
Unbelievable...

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:20.500
To think that I would be able to play
hide-and-seek with a real Kin like this...!

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:38.830
Help me!!

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:41.700
We've got you now!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:42.000
Help me!!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.200
Hey, #4, hurry and help me tie this
thing up! It keeps thrashing around!
Help me!!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.400
Hey, #4, hurry and help me tie this
thing up! It keeps thrashing around!

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:46.500
Sure.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:47.100
Help me!!
Sure.

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:47.790
Help me!!

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.740
Right, this should do it.

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:57.200
Let me out! Why are you doing this?!

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.700
What's going on here?

00:13:03.060 --> 00:13:08.400
The Grey Guards caught a young Kin while I was playing hide-and-seek with it.

00:13:08.780 --> 00:13:10.700
You played hide-and-seek with a Kin...?

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.300
Unbelievable...

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:16.400
We're having a feast for today's breakfast!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:18.900
You sure this thing is edible?

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:24.700
Of course it's edible! Don't you
see how fat and juicy it is?

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:34.200
To think that we would find this spring so soon after
drinking the last of our water. Today sure is our lucky day!

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:48.300
I thought this was going to be a simple job of transporting prisoners, but that lot had to get in our way...

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.900
Seems like they were after Glock and Neridah.

00:13:52.850 --> 00:13:56.800
And it seems like Doom was able
to save them, just as he promised.

00:13:57.680 --> 00:14:00.400
We'll catch them again before the sun sets.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:04.200
Let's teach them a lesson they
won't forget when we get them.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:04.910
Of course.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:09.510
Mum! Save me! Mum!

00:14:10.200 --> 00:14:11.680
Shut your damned mouth!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:12.000
-Ouch!
Shut your damned mouth!

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:12.440
-Ouch!

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.700
This is unforgivable...!

00:14:22.540 --> 00:14:23.300
What was that?!

00:14:23.640 --> 00:14:24.980
Let's check it out.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:25.440
Yeah!

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.300
Now!

00:14:33.210 --> 00:14:34.740
I'm here to save you, Prin!

00:14:34.740 --> 00:14:36.200
Lief! Please help!

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:37.200
Keep your voice down!

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:39.300
There's nothing here...

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.100
I'm sure it came from this way, though...

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.700
There, that did it!

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:47.820
Lief!

00:14:48.390 --> 00:14:49.200
Prin!

00:14:51.230 --> 00:14:52.200
Hey you!

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:01.140
Oh no...! I didn't bring my sword!

00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:05.640
Wait, aren't you...? I see, you're one of the others from Rithmere that got away, aren't you?

00:15:06.160 --> 00:15:07.820
Lief... I'm scared...

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:10.570
Don't worry, I'm here with you.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:12.450
You sure talk big for an unarmed boy!

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:28.700
They... turned into trees...?

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.400
That I was not expecting.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:36.000
"All of evil will beware"...

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:40.200
So that's why the trees here are so silent...

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.120
Look! Those boulders are moving!

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:58.090
That's quite rude of you. That's my Mum and the others! They're just waking up from their sleep!

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:00.280
It really talks!

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:01.700
Prin!

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.400
Mum!

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.500
They're... All of them are real Kin...!

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.950
I am the Kin Elder, Crenn.

00:16:25.950 --> 00:16:32.100
Allow me to express my gratitude for saving our young Prin from danger.

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.120
Thank you all so much for saving my child.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:38.720
The one who saved your child was him; Lief.

00:16:40.380 --> 00:16:41.800
Lief, Lief!

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:42.570
Prin!

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:46.120
He's right! Lief is my best friend, after all!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:50.830
Prin, have you forgotten that you were almost kidnapped by those evil men?

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:57.520
It was no problem! Those guys drank from the spring,
after all! I knew that they were going to turn into trees!

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:01.200
Although, we also drank from that spring.

00:17:01.600 --> 00:17:05.200
Did you not read what was engraved on the plate?

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:12.200
Good guys will never be harmed. The water from the spring only harms the bad!

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:17.520
All that aside, I never would have expected
to encounter the Kin species on my travels...

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:24.400
Our numbers have diminished greatly after we left that mountain, that is for sure.

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.800
By 'that mountain', do you mean Dread Mountain?

00:17:30.180 --> 00:17:31.700
Correct.

00:17:31.700 --> 00:17:36.100
Apart from ourselves, there is a race that lives there called the Dread Gnomes.

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:41.200
The Dread Gnomes were always trying to hunt our kind with bows and arrows.

00:17:41.200 --> 00:17:46.800
However, their arrows were far from being strong enough to harm us.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:53.200
That is, until one day they started to dip their arrows in poison, you see...

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:59.600
And with that deadly poison, they began to slaughter the Kin one after another.

00:18:00.560 --> 00:18:08.100
We who survived the ordeal discussed the matter at length before finally deciding to leave Dread Mountain for good.

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:16.900
And nowadays, drinking the water from this spring and dreaming is our only means of attaining happiness.

00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:19.380
And what do you see in those dreams?

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:21.300
The Boolong trees, I heard.

00:18:22.030 --> 00:18:30.450
You see, there is a place called the Boolong Forest in Dread Mountain, where the air is sweet and a beautiful river flows.

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:36.900
And for us currently, the only way to see that sight again is through our dreams.

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:42.100
But at least you live happily in this new place, right?

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:46.910
We are happy, but at the same time, we aren't.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:52.800
We Kin cannot breed without
eating the cones of the Boolong trees.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:58.400
Prin was actually the last child to
be born after we moved here.

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:04.300
And as long as the Dread Gnomes
have their poison arrows,

00:19:04.300 --> 00:19:07.280
returning to Dread Mountain
would be as good as suicide.

00:19:07.280 --> 00:19:11.390
But I want to see and eat the Boolong cones too!

00:19:11.390 --> 00:19:14.370
It's not fair that only the adults got to eat it!

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:19.300
But Prin, dreams won't always
bring you happiness, you know.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:23.550
In my case, the dream that I
had last night was really weird!

00:19:23.860 --> 00:19:25.100
What kind of weird dream?

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:30.500
It was a dream about Doom. Of all the things to
dream about, why did it have to be of that guy...?

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:36.700
So you three aren't aware of it, then. Those dreams that you had here are in fact a reality.

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:39.300
What do you mean by that?

00:19:39.810 --> 00:19:45.300
When you drink the water from the Dreaming Spring, your soul will temporarily leave your body,

00:19:45.300 --> 00:19:48.210
and visit the people or places you truly wish to see.

00:19:48.650 --> 00:19:52.250
That's not funny! There's no way
that I'd actually want to see Doom!

00:19:52.980 --> 00:19:58.400
So, Manus and the other Ralads that I saw in my dream are safe in real world too, then...

00:19:59.820 --> 00:20:01.920
If that dream was actually true...

00:20:04.280 --> 00:20:06.300
Then that mark of the Shadowlord...

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.000
Lief?

00:20:09.400 --> 00:20:10.300
What's the matter?

00:20:10.920 --> 00:20:11.990
I have to go back...!

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:12.100
Lief!

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.110
-Lief!
Lief!

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:14.900
What's gotten into you?!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.030
I wonder what happened to Lief...

00:20:20.000 --> 00:20:21.300
Lief, wait!

00:20:24.740 --> 00:20:27.150
Where are you going, Lief?

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.100
I'm going back home.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.200
Home...?

00:20:37.400 --> 00:20:41.100
Jarred and Anna... you dreamt of them, didn't you?

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:46.100
I saw our home last night...

00:20:48.030 --> 00:20:51.710
It was empty and looked as if it had been ransacked...

00:20:51.710 --> 00:20:55.700
And what's more... I saw the
Shadow Lord's brand on the front door!

00:20:57.860 --> 00:21:01.620
That's why I have to go back! Right now!!

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:02.700
Lief.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:05.500
And what of your mission?!

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:09.440
My mother and father are
in dire trouble right now...!

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:12.620
How can you expect me to do nothing?!

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:17.200
Do you really think that Jarred and Anna would be happy if you returned now?!

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:21.910
Do you really think that they would welcome you back, after you threw your mission aside?!

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:27.800
We are going on this journey in those two's stead.

00:21:28.620 --> 00:21:29.920
Do <i>not</i> forget that!

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:35.700
Father...

00:21:37.300 --> 00:21:38.400
And even Mother...

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:43.400
So they were both intending on
gathering the seven gems themselves...?

00:21:47.710 --> 00:21:48.500
Barda.

00:21:51.500 --> 00:21:52.700
I apologise.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.800
You're right... They would both surely want me to continue this journey.

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:01.770
That's right.

00:22:04.320 --> 00:22:09.700
Rather, I have no choice but to go on... That is the nature of my mission!

00:22:10.790 --> 00:22:12.700
That's right, Lief.

00:22:13.430 --> 00:22:17.560
Alright, with that settled, let's continue on our way to Dread Mountain!

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:18.300
Yeah.

00:22:18.950 --> 00:22:20.300
Hold on just a moment.

00:22:21.610 --> 00:22:24.600
Regarding that, I actually have a little plan.

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:27.710
A little plan...?

00:22:48.510 --> 00:22:51.050
On nights when a gentle breeze caresses your cheek

00:22:51.050 --> 00:22:53.550
And you start walking with your head held high

00:22:53.550 --> 00:22:57.680
You might just be blessed by the big red sun

00:22:57.930 --> 00:23:00.310
When hardships cause you to stumble

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:02.770
And you keep hanging your head in shame

00:23:03.020 --> 00:23:07.820
Just know that you may end up missing out on that one emotional scene

00:23:08.650 --> 00:23:10.610
The Earth, with all of its living things

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:13.240
The sea, sky and sun: seven days of grace

00:23:13.570 --> 00:23:15.990
Not noticing how thirsty I had become

00:23:15.990 --> 00:23:18.410
I turned my back on this town and walked away

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:23.670
If you've searched near and far but still can't find the answer to your problem

00:23:23.710 --> 00:23:28.050
Before you give up, take a step forward with a bit of courage towards a new chapter

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.550
Let's write a new page

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:33.090
Take my hand, come on, we're gonna go

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:38.180
Whether you're up or down, it's just one second! Get up! Stand up!

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:40.730
Let's write a new page

00:23:41.430 --> 00:23:43.230
Take my hand, come on, we're gonna go

00:23:44.020 --> 00:23:48.360
Whether you're laughing or crying, it's just once. Get up! Stand up!

00:24:04.770 --> 00:24:06.780
The Deltora Encyclopedia

00:24:06.780 --> 00:24:07.500
<i>Kin.
The Deltora Encyclopedia</i>

00:24:07.500 --> 00:24:08.270
The Deltora Encyclopedia

00:24:08.760 --> 00:24:11.700
<i>A legendary animal that was said to be extinct.</i>

00:24:12.020 --> 00:24:14.420
<i>They have wings that enable flight.</i>

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:19.400
<i>The females have a pouch on their stomachs, which they use to carry their young.</i>

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:26.220
We, who have become good friends with Prin,
finally continue our journey to Dread Mountain!

00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:30.820
Are you ready, Barda? That look really suits you.

00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:31.100
Fly, Kin. To the Air!
Are you ready, Barda? That look really suits you.

